## 7. Rider Dashboard Fake Stats

**Root Cause:** [RiderDashboard.jsx](file:///c:/Users/gikiw/OneDrive/Desktop/NaanNow/frontend/src/pages/RiderDashboard/RiderDashboard.jsx#L182-L187) initializes stats with hardcoded values `{ todayEarnings: 450, tripsCount: 3, tipsAmount: 120, rating: 4.9 }`. The [useEffect on line 247](file:///c:/Users/gikiw/OneDrive/Desktop/NaanNow/frontend/src/pages/RiderDashboard/RiderDashboard.jsx#L247-L259) also adds `450` and `3` as base offsets on top of real data.

**Fix:** Initialize stats to zero and compute them purely from actual completed orders.

#### [MODIFY] [RiderDashboard.jsx](file:///c:/Users/gikiw/OneDrive/Desktop/NaanNow/frontend/src/pages/RiderDashboard/RiderDashboard.jsx)
- Change initial stats to `{ todayEarnings: 0, tripsCount: 0, tipsAmount: 0, rating: 0 }`
- In the `useEffect`, compute stats from `completedOrders` without adding hardcoded offsets
- Use `currentUser.rating` from the database for the rating field

